cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "gs-dipi: Decomposing South African Inflation into External and Domestic Components"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kyle
    family-names: Ferreira
    email: kyle.fe0212@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/KyleFe/gs-dipi"
abstract: >-
  An ARDL-based decomposition of South African headline CPI inflation into the
  contributions of the nominal effective exchange rate, Brent crude and global
  food prices, leaving a residual Domestic Inflationary Pressure Index (DIPI)
  used as a proxy for underlying domestic price pressure. Includes rolling-window
  time-varying pass-through estimation, impulse-response decomposition,
  hold-constant projections and oil shock scenario analysis.
keywords:
  - inflation
  - South Africa
  - ARDL
  - exchange rate pass-through
  - macroeconometrics
  - monetary policy
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
